                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Disclaimer: My scores/reviews are almost always based on having bought the game at close to the \"lowest historical price\" on steam at time of purchase.\n\nQuick score: 3/5\n\nNotes: The game starts off pretty good, but by the end it feels like development was cut way short of what was initially planned. The story feels about 25% complete and ends very abruptly, but in terms of gameplay it is relatively polished and enjoyable, just don't expect to be blown away.\n\nThe biggest issue I experienced is that the game is broken on hard difficulty, there are 3-4 rooms that softlock your game if you are playing on hard mode and the only solution I found was to quit to menu, switch difficulty to normal, clear the room, switch back to hard and continue. What happens is that you will clear a \"wave\" of enemies and the next wave will just never spawn. Also a minor issue, the UI for changing difficulty is broken visually but it does function, wont bother explaining.\n\nThere is a game called \"RIVE\" on steam that is very similar in terms of gameplay which I would highly recommend over this.\n\nIn the end this game isn't bad, and it was enjoyable (outside of the softlocks) for the 90-120 minutes of gameplay it offers. But there are many many better games, RIVE being the closest superior alternative.",
